Author:     kara <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Mon Nov 16 10:20:24 2026 -0500
Commit:     kara <totalwindupflightsystems@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Mon Nov 16 10:20:24 2026 -0500

    fix(mcp): add events.processed migration so the SSE poll query stops throwing SQLITE_ERROR (DF-SPECLANG-4-R4)
    
    The SSE manager's poll loop queries
      SELECT * FROM events WHERE timestamp > ? AND processed = 0 ORDER BY timestamp LIMIT 10
    but `events` was created without a `processed` column, so better-sqlite3 raised
    `SQLITE_ERROR: no such column: processed`. Because pollChanges() wraps the poll in
    try/catch, the failure was silent: no file-change event was ever broadcast.
    
    Fix: keep the query and give the schema the column it asks for.
    - migrations.ts: new migration `version: 2, name: 'add_events_processed'` that runs
      `ALTER TABLE events ADD COLUMN processed INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` plus
      `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_events_processed_timestamp ON events(processed, timestamp)`.
      It flows through the existing `migrate()` gate (`version > getCurrentVersion()`), so an
      existing version-1 database is upgraded on the next initialize(), not just a fresh one.
    - The committed compiled artifacts next to the source (migrations.js / .js.map / .d.ts.map)
      were regenerated in place because the specs/*.spec.dir tree is what the test runner and
      runtime actually load (`./migrations.js` resolves to the physical .js, which shadows the
      .ts). Emitted with the same flags the committed artifacts used, so the diff is the new
      migration block plus the source-map lines only.
    
    Tests:
    - tests/mcp.test.ts: new case under "SSE Module" — opens a freshly migrated temp DB,
      inserts two `events` rows, flips one to processed = 1, then drives the SSE poll and
      asserts it does not throw and broadcasts only the unprocessed row.
      RED-proven: with migrations.ts reverted it fails with `SqliteError: no such column: processed`.
    - tests/db.test.ts: migration-count assertions updated 1 -> 2 (four call sites).
    
    Gates: npx vitest run tests/mcp.test.ts 33/33 pass; tests/db.test.ts 35/35 pass;
    npx tsc --noEmit exit 0; npm run build exit 0.
